WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.213
Unit 3 is what the ISSO receives.

2
00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:05.523
Each run is packaged: the run itself,

3
00:00:05.523 --> 00:00:10.465
a summary with rule I D's and fingerprints
but no names, an evidence manifest,

4
00:00:10.465 --> 00:00:14.450
and a checksum file anyone can
verify with the standard tool.

5
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:19.044
Before it writes anything, the
packager checks the run end to end:

6
00:00:19.044 --> 00:00:23.725
every manifest by its hash, nothing
extra, one tenant and one cloud.

7
00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:28.485
Each package records the previous
package's manifest hash, so the packages

8
00:00:28.485 --> 00:00:32.862
form a chain, and a replaced package
or a missing day shows up as a break.

9
00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:35.423
Then the period verifies every package,

10
00:00:35.423 --> 00:00:39.537
checks the chain and coverage,
and maps findings to each control.

11
00:00:39.537 --> 00:00:42.409
There's no signing, by
the kit's design: hashes,

12
00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:46.636
plus a locked time-based retention
policy on the evidence store,

13
00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:51.501
the write once, read many storage
Microsoft Learn documents for blob data.

14
00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.349
Each control reads
either evidence present,

15
00:00:54.349 --> 00:00:57.275
the assessor decides,
or evidence incomplete.

16
00:00:57.275 --> 00:01:00.580
The control mapping is the
program's design guidance.
